      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that clarification. my biggest headache right now is actually the preservation side of this. we have these small, unsorted bundles of papers and fragments that arrived in a single crate, and they're basically just a chaotic jumble right now. it feels like once we start cataloging, we're going to find all these little \"nuisances\" or weird bits that just disrupt the flow of a clean system. do you have any advice for managing that initial stage of organization so the chaos doesn't just spread through the whole archive as we go?",
